From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: abort suspend when a device has signalled PME

pcie_pme_suspend() keeps the Root Port's PME interrupt armed only if it
can wake the system. On SC8280XP it is an MSI through the GIC ITS, which
can't, so the interrupt is disabled from the port's suspend callback on.
A PME that a wakeup-enabled endpoint sends after that point is never
handled: nothing aborts the suspend, and dw_pcie_suspend_noirq()
broadcasts PME_Turn_Off to an endpoint that has just asked to wake the
system.

The WCN6855 Wi-Fi of the Huawei MateBook E Go does exactly this with
WoWLAN when a packet matches a wake pattern during suspend entry, after
it was put in D3hot. In a test with a wake-on-TCP pattern and packets
arriving at random times, PME Status was set before PME_Turn_Off in 6 of
11 suspends; 4 of those 6 never got PME_TO_Ack ("Timeout waiting for L2
entry", LTSSM in L0), and none of the other 5 timed out. Waiting 200 ms
instead of 10 ms made no difference. The link is powered down after the
timeout anyway, and after a few of these the endpoint no longer came
back on resume.

Check the Root Status PME bit before PME_Turn_Off. When it is set,
report a wakeup on the requester, as the PME service would, and fail the
suspend with -EBUSY. The PCI core clears the bit on resume. The first
version of this change, which only failed the suspend, aborted 130 of
150 suspends in the same test, with no timeout and no lost link; this
version aborted 2 in about 140 suspends on the same machine.

A PME from a device that isn't enabled for wakeup aborts the suspend
too: the PME_Turn_Off hazard doesn't depend on that setting. A
wakeup-enabled device that keeps sending PME keeps the system from
suspending, as it would where the PME interrupt can wake the system.
Not covered: a PME that reaches the Root Port between the check and
PME_Turn_Off.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c | 43 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
index dbcd360bb..4a82418b2 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
@@ -1226,10 +1226,28 @@ static int dw_pcie_pme_turn_off(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Return the requester ID of a PME that the Root Port received and nothing has
+ * handled, or -1. For system suspend, pcie_pme_suspend() turns the PME
+ * interrupt off unless it can wake the system, which an MSI through a GIC ITS
+ * can't. The PCI core clears the bit on resume, see
+ * pcie_pme_root_status_cleanup().
+ */
+static int dw_pcie_pme_received(struct dw_pcie *pci)
+{
+	u8 offset = dw_pcie_find_capability(pci, PCI_CAP_ID_EXP);
+	u32 val = dw_pcie_readl_dbi(pci, offset + PCI_EXP_RTSTA);
+
+	if (PCI_POSSIBLE_ERROR(val) || !(val & PCI_EXP_RTSTA_PME))
+		return -1;
+
+	return FIELD_GET(PCI_EXP_RTSTA_PME_RQ_ID, val);
+}
+
 int dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 {
 	bool pme_capable = false;
-	int ret = 0;
+	int ret = 0, rid;
 	u32 val;
 
 	pci->link_up_at_suspend = dw_pcie_link_up(pci);
@@ -1239,6 +1257,29 @@ int dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	if (!pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(pci->pp.bridge, &pme_capable))
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * A device has asked to wake the system. Turning the link off now
+	 * races with that: an endpoint that has just sent PME may never
+	 * acknowledge PME_Turn_Off, and powering it down regardless can leave
+	 * it unable to bring the link back. Abort the suspend instead, and
+	 * report the wakeup on the device as the PME service would have.
+	 */
+	rid = dw_pcie_pme_received(pci);
+	if (rid >= 0) {
+		int domain = pci_domain_nr(pci->pp.bridge->bus);
+		struct pci_dev *pdev;
+
+		pdev = pci_get_domain_bus_and_slot(domain, PCI_BUS_NUM(rid),
+						   rid & 0xff);
+		if (pdev) {
+			pci_wakeup_event(pdev);
+			pci_dev_put(pdev);
+		}
+		dev_info(pci->dev, "PME from %02x:%02x.%d, aborting suspend\n",
+			 PCI_BUS_NUM(rid), PCI_SLOT(rid), PCI_FUNC(rid));
+		return -EBUSY;
+	}
+
 	if (pci->pp.ops->pme_turn_off) {
 		pci->pp.ops->pme_turn_off(&pci->pp);
 	} else {
